UgyLUZ6uLB5ab53zVdB4AaABAg,,False,@oreofisk,"I want to love BTS as much as I did when I first found them. I feel like I don’t get sad at their emotional videos anymore. I remember crying for 5 days when I saw an imagine of them. I am sad I can’t love them as much as I want. I’m afraid my love for them will decrease. I am afraid I’ll start ignoring them. Unfortunately, I can’t love them as much as I want and need to keep it to a certain level. This loving is now titled as “obsession” in my country. I just wish I could love them to the end of the world, till my afterlife. This will be hard. I want to love them more. I want to love them so much that I cry when they explain us a sad, but funny incident. Now that I’m reading this, I am tearing up. Why? I’m tearing up because BTS gave me so much without me realising and I can’t pay them back. You won’t imagine how much they’ve been through and how much we’ve been through with them, without realising. BTS healed me. I don’t have suicidal thoughts now. I never paid attention to how and when things changed when they came into my life, I just loved them with my heart. Now I realise: how much important and dear BTS are to me. Their music is beautiful, sometimes sad and sometimes enthusiastic. Their lyrics relate to me. Their life relates to me, too. They relate to me a lot. They are my type and that’s why I chose to stan them. I remember searching for them 6 days after my birthday because they were trending a lot back then when DNA came out. I will never regret how that was the best birthday gift I ever got. It hits hard, it’s been 7 years already. Run era specially makes me nostalgic. I love BTS so much. Thank you for everything, BTS. Even this paragraph of emotional thoughts isn’t enough. There are thousands of reasons I love you. Thank you for existing. Love, all the ARMY.",0,2020-06-13T12:37:22Z,2020-06-13T12:37:22Z
