UgyD2oNvmq1NQQQu4cZ4AaABAg.99gLM2nzvLD99gM456O5mx,UgyD2oNvmq1NQQQu4cZ4AaABAg,True,@attyimelda22,"Not just Korean girls. They appeal to girls of all nationalities.  Hard to say one particular point of attraction. As the saying goes, beauty is in the eye of the beholder. To each his own.",0,2020-06-09T13:40:38Z,2020-06-09T22:10:09Z
UgyD2oNvmq1NQQQu4cZ4AaABAg.99gLM2nzvLD99gMq-7Np3I,UgyD2oNvmq1NQQQu4cZ4AaABAg,True,@KHINEKOOKOO,"It’s Korean girls find them attractive.  They have fans all over the world. And they were not popular in their home country Korea first. Irony is started popular in US first. 
Why do they become popular? Many reason. But, mostly is their lyrics, their vocal color and ranges. They have 3 rappers who are way better than most Korean idol group rappers. 
Many of their lyrics have metaphors and referencing to psychology books, literature, Greek mythology. Their MVs have hint to next song or album. They do have parallel universe story theme. Some of the songs are not random but part of the story. For example, Love Yourself album has seven solo songs of BTS members and they portray seven stages of love. 
And they don’t stick to one music genre. Even in one song, there’re more than two genres. 
Unless you dig up all their performances, songs, MVs, you’ll not get an idea. BTS topic is quite big. What I can say is they are not ordinary music band. Many things contributed to their success.
Are they attractive? Yes ... May be you can check out “Singularity” and “Agust D” and “Mic Drop” MVs. They  have energetic songs as well as delicate songs. 
These three songs are soft version/delicate side (more feminine) songs. 
But, Outro Tear (rap song), Not Today, Dionysus and even Mic Drop are more masculine/hard songs.",1,2020-06-09T13:47:19Z,2020-06-09T13:51:56Z
