Ugy8-_1JekVPwJ-aejp4AaABAg,,False,@jackiearnolds,"Omg I didn't even know this was happening. In the country I live, school year goes with the year, so from February to December instead of September to June, so people in regular school and most people in college aren't graduating that soon and will likely be able to have their ceremonies performed, as they often occur months after (if you finish college in mid-December, you're ceremony will happen in between January to March). But I was one of those people who were only able to get to college late in the year, which means I will be graduating in June instead of December, with just a couple more weeks of class to go, for a matter of fact. It's really sad for me that I won't be able to get my family and friends together to celebrate me finally graduating after all the struggle I went through in these years. I know this weren't exactly made with people like me in mind, but it does warms my heart and brings me some comfort nonetheless. Thank you so much for this. It makes me feel better in these hard times. Thank you.",58,2020-06-09T02:57:02Z,2020-06-09T02:57:02Z
