UgzLlfqa5HI4kekPaJl4AaABAg.99e_w7hQBlZ99eeofoVPhg,UgzLlfqa5HI4kekPaJl4AaABAg,True,@GSCTHADON,"Serena 沁 R not gonna argue with you. But as a man in the music industry this happens to frequently. You may not question what is happening behind the scenes but as a man I wouldn’t want to be wearing lipstick and makeup or painting my nails.. plus 80% of the listeners are children, we shouldn’t be letting the kids watch men look like women and women look like men that’s what’s “sad”",0,2020-06-08T21:54:41Z,2020-06-08T21:54:41Z
UgzLlfqa5HI4kekPaJl4AaABAg.99e_w7hQBlZ99ephyMl0oF,UgzLlfqa5HI4kekPaJl4AaABAg,True,@yooniecola3123,"Gabriel Cruz 
I apologize if my tone sounded like arguing, but I’ve just heard too many people saying “they look like girls...” as if it was an insult. Six years ago, they already faced this insult when talking to another person, and it was surely pointless.

I think I understand where you are coming from, but I have to disagree. I think it is okay for men to where makeup to freshen up, it is fine if they use makeup to touch up on their appearance, and it is okay for them to dress up in pastel colors etc. Some of the fans actually like them for that (redefining masculinity) I personally don’t have a preference and I think BTS doesn’t mind either, anyways, all because they wear makeup doesn’t automatically make them more feminine, they are masculine and powerful in their own ways, and I know it is common in the Kpop industry. In my opinion, not all men have to be under the stereotype of “I don’t wear makeup” or “I have to look harsh and cool” or “If I paint nails, I am girly.” I think it would be more sad if children grow up thinking they have to look a certain way and be a certain way. I don’t want boys to be scared to be girlier, prettier or cute, and I don’t want girls to be scared to be a tomboy, sporty, masculine etc.

I hope I made my point, if we still disagree, I suppose we simply have different morals and values in life, which is fine.",0,2020-06-08T23:29:53Z,2020-06-08T23:29:53Z
