UgyCfuOAPJYf9m1XAq54AaABAg,,False,@Jimin-ci4ed,"I am really graduating this year and I found bts in first grade, it's been 6 years  and they have been with me all the time, when I felt happy, sad, discouraged, alone, lost, insecure or afraid of the future. There was always a song to make me happy, they vidéos made me laugh for hours I even learnt English thanks to them, by watching them. Sometimes I was feeling some kind of way and they dropped songs with lyrics I could relate to. These little coincidences made me feel so happy. I grew up with them and as I was growing their music was evolving and they were growing up along side with me. They are the only  that make me feel like this, like we lived something together, even tho I never met them or even stepped on the same ground as them lol. This is the connection that I as an Army feel, I'm really thankful to them for being here and being the way they are, they are artists and I am just a 19 years old girl  now but  somehow we were linked by music they helped me even tho they don't know  how much and I hope I also helped them at least a little bit.

Next year I am going to university but  in a way or another I hope we can still be together...
And maybe one day meet and hear our voices in real life through an unforgettable concert.

Let's continue to stay strong together thank you bts,
With love , ARMY",3,2020-06-08T17:41:46Z,2020-06-08T17:41:46Z
