Ugwot7Y6IDWbtvjYNcJ4AaABAg,,False,@caramajor4175,"I found bts at the beginning of my freshman year. When my family decided to leave from my hometown, where I'd grown up for the past 10 years, and move to California, Spring Day and So Far Away got me through the last week's I spent there. I cried every time I listened go them. After we moved, I didn't have anyone. The people at school I went to seemed not to even notice I was there and we had no family around that we could see. We were all alone. I became very suicidal and depressed. I developed bad social anxiety and anxiety in general. BTS became my rock during that time. Watching them and learning about them gave me an escape from my brain and everything I hated about my life. They were there for me.
The following year I moved to a nearby town, where we had made friends and felt more at home. I started my junior year in this small town, this small school of only 38 students and I made some of the best friends I could ever ask for. I made myself do things I would have never done before and I found the biggest joy in supporting this newfound family.
My senior year could have been better. Way better. But I grew more than ever before and to this day I'm so thankful for BTS and the things they gave me. Reasons to love myself. The courage to be who I am. Strength to fight through the hardest times of my life and find happiness. When they performed Spring Day, I started to cry. It was as if they knew how much it meant to me, still means to me. As if they knew how hard I had fought for my life those past few years. 
Thank you for making me feel seen Bangtan. I love each and every one of you and I wish you as much happiness as you have inspired so many people around the world. 💜",146,2020-06-08T17:02:36Z,2020-06-08T17:02:36Z
Ugwot7Y6IDWbtvjYNcJ4AaABAg.99e8OPpb77H99eB5lVShn_,Ugwot7Y6IDWbtvjYNcJ4AaABAg,True,@Sabrina-rina3,💜💜💜💜,1,2020-06-08T17:26:16Z,2020-06-08T17:26:16Z
Ugwot7Y6IDWbtvjYNcJ4AaABAg.99e8OPpb77H99eB7PxYP9I,Ugwot7Y6IDWbtvjYNcJ4AaABAg,True,@raneemiftekhar6354,"Reading this made me emotional, I totally understand. I have kind of a very similar story. I’ve moved a lot, more than 10 times and two years ago that sense of sadness and feeling incomplete caught up to me. I was in the end of eighth grade , and I hated my life so much. I felt like it was hopeless to make friends because every time I had to leave. I found BTS during that time, and it was almost crazy how much pure happiness they gave me. The only time I remember smiling and feeling joy on that school campus was the day Fake Love came out and I was listening to the whole album while walking. Then high school started, I moved to a school with only 30 students in each grade and the community I found there meant so much to me. I threw myself into getting to know my classmates, getting  involved in sports and theater and I felt like I had truly found my place. Then last October, the unthinkable happened and the school announced their permanent closure this year( its been open since 1961).  Accepting this has been the hardest thing in my life to deal with, and the pandemic stealing our last months together only made it worse. At the start of quarantine,  I listened to So Far Away and cried so so hard.  I still am having a hard time. This weekend was graduation and school’s official closure. I went home after feeling numb and really sad, jealous of the seniors who got to graduate. I’ve decided to leave high school early and go to community college next year  , but I felt bitter that I would never get a proper high school graduation. The next day, I was watching this in bed and hearing them sing Spring Day really gave me chills. It’s like they know what we’re going through.",4,2020-06-08T17:26:29Z,2020-06-08T17:26:29Z
Ugwot7Y6IDWbtvjYNcJ4AaABAg.99e8OPpb77H99eBq20bjKO,Ugwot7Y6IDWbtvjYNcJ4AaABAg,True,@isabelpenaloza4351,😔✋,1,2020-06-08T17:32:43Z,2020-06-08T17:32:43Z
Ugwot7Y6IDWbtvjYNcJ4AaABAg.99e8OPpb77H99eCLjRElAE,Ugwot7Y6IDWbtvjYNcJ4AaABAg,True,@caramajor4175,"@@raneemiftekhar6354 you have so much strength in you to be able to come this far, I don't know you but I feel so proud that you've pressed on. I'm sure your classmates were so blessed to have you and see you every day. We don't realize how much of an impact we have on each other until we are able to stop and look back, I hope you're able to see the beauty you brought to that place. 
We are all in this together <3 Keep your head up high and feet moving forward. I hope you make the most of these difficult times and you find the purest happiness again. 💜",1,2020-06-08T17:37:11Z,2020-06-08T17:37:11Z
